<title>EGYPT: Egypt gives phone companies more time to prequalif.</title>
<headline>Egypt gives phone companies more time to prequalif.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state telephone authority said on Friday it was extending until February 1 the deadline for companies to apply to prequalify for licences to instal and operate public payphones.</p>
<p>The original deadline was January 25.</p>
<p>The National Telecommunications Organisation (ARENTO) says it plans to issue two such licences. It will be the first time private-sector companies have been able to run telephone services in Egypt.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
